    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_32468f177f7e9661b0159ed4a87bdc5338a9669b912570b7ae79fac50869d32c",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The real-part estimate used to exclude derivative zeros also acquires a geometric meaning: through the logarithmic-derivative identity, its sign is the horizontal derivative of log modulus, so the RH-conditional estimate yields leftward growth of the derivative's modulus. At sufficiently large height in the critical strip, the source states the converse as well, upgrading the sign from a proof device to an RH-equivalent monotonicity criterion within the stated range.",
