    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_899271456abc792353eff2aa06b32c889672c4627cf56a8234ab5d3d69fbe3a4",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Analytic boundary estimates first remove the unbounded far-left tail and confine possible derivative zeros to three bounded regions; the source then changes computational representation by region, using Euler–Maclaurin where direct evaluation is suitable, gamma-logarithmic-derivative asymptotics farther left, and recurrence translations near the origin. The finite reduction and representation-specific numerical plan are successive parts of one certification strategy.",
